# 🎯 ONE-LINE EXAM ANSWER

> **Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) is a vulnerability in which an attacker causes an authenticated user's browser to send an unintended state-changing request to a target application; defenses include server-side CSRF tokens, appropriate SameSite cookie policies, origin validation, safe HTTP method design, and secure authentication architecture.**